  "term": "labyrinthitis",
  "definition": "Labyrinthitis is inflammation of the inner ear caused by an infection, most often a viral one. It commonly brings severe dizziness, nausea, vomiting, pain, and sometimes anxiety, and it often follows a recent upper respiratory infection.",
